T*
() Tj
T*
(The main risk is not a missing Super Admin role check. The main risk is context leakage:) Tj
T*
(  Super Admin can scope into a tenant by setting `selectedOrganizationId`, and the API) Tj
T*
(  interceptor then sends `x-organization-id` automatically. One organization detail/edit) Tj
T*
(  route sets this selected organization but does not clean it up, so later global Super) Tj
T*
(  Admin pages can behave as if they are still inside that tenant.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The second major risk is server-side tenant route strictness. The frontend prevents many) Tj
T*
(  unsafe calls, but shared tenant APIs should still reject Super Admin requests without an) Tj
T*
(  explicit organization scope. At least the users API can return a platform-wide user list) Tj
T*
(  to a Super Admin if called without a selected organization.) Tj
